so today we're talking about battlefield  2042 getting hit with a delay how you  can finally connect bluetooth headphones  to your switch and how the developers of  split gate are just swimming in a pool  full of money my name is devonte  chisholm and you're watching gamespot  news originally slated for release on  october 22nd battlefield 2042 will now  arrive on november 19th ea said the  teams did not have the opportunity to  get back together in person to work on  finishing the game and that this meant  extra time was needed before it would be  ready the game is now releasing very  close to halo infinite though it's now  coming a few weeks after call of duty  vanguard instead of right before it so  far it's already been a long road to  release for battlefield 2042 as dice  took an extra year with the game to give  developers more time to make the most of  the ps5 and xbox series x and s the game  supports 128 players on those platforms  compared to the 64 on ps4 and xbox one  and now let's talk about nintendo late  last night switch owners got a big  surprise when it was announced that  bluetooth audio output was finally added  in a new firmware update a feature that  many fans have been requesting since the  console's launch and i want to stress  the word output because bluetooth  microphones are not supported and  additionally bluetooth audio won't work  when the switch's local wireless  connection is running some other changes  included in the update are the ability  to stay connected to the internet in  sleep mode when using a wired connection  a new way to start the control stick  calibration process and the ability to  connect up to two wireless controllers  when using bluetooth better late than  never i guess but i do feel kind of bad  for the people who bought the third  party piece to make the bluetooth  possible even though that does have less  limitations than the official update so  i guess it wasn't a waste of money  yesterday the developer of the popular  halo meets portal multiplayer shooter  split gate announced it has raised 100  million dollars in funding to help  support its ambitions let me say that  again  100 million dollars in a statement ceo  ian prow said quote i'm happy to confirm  that we are not selling our company to  one of the big guys instead 1047 games  will stay independent and continue to be  a quote community first game developer  the 100 million dollars in funding will  help 1047 games hire a lot more  developers and this in turn will help  the team deliver more and better updates  to split gate this will also help the  studio fix bugs faster and support a  wider base of players overall 1047 games  is now valued at 1.5 billion according  to games industry.biz  and in some gaming related news mcu star  anthony mackie is set to play the lead  character john doe in an upcoming tv  series based on twisted metal as  announced previously deadpool writers  rhett reese and paul wernick came up  with the idea for the show and cobra  kai's michael jonathan smith is writing  according to deadline the producers at  sony pictures tv and playstations  productions are quote extremely high on  the show and will begin to shop it  around to network soon deadline also has  the details on the tv show's story it  will follow mackie who is a quote  motor mouth outsider offered a chance at  a better life but only if he can  successfully deliver a mysterious  package across a post-apocalyptic  wasteland  in the comment section let me know on a  scale of 1 to 10 how bummed you are  about the battlefield delay  and hopefully we don't get another game  delay in tomorrow's video  peace  [Music]  you
 

